  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Refactor routing to IRoutable and remove transport bases:\n      - Introduce IRoutable and migrate handler routing to a unified routable model.\n      - HandlerBase signatures were changed to accept IRoutable and SessionTransport (ResolveRoute, CanHandle), BuildKey was reimplemented to extract method/path from IRoutable.UrlRoute/MethodRoute, and invoker delegates/RouteEntry types were updated to use IRoutable/SessionTransport.\n      - Parameter type discovery now inspects [Data]/[Session] parameters instead of IHandler<,> interfaces and validates types. SimulationManager.DispatchCore now constrains T to IRoutable and PooledObject, uses IRoutableEvent (RoutableEvent<>) factories, and sets event.data/event.session when enqueuing.\n      - Removed several transport-specific handler base classes (HttpHandlerBase, HttpsHandlerBase, WsHandlerBase, WssHandlerBase) and renamed IHandler.cs to IRoutable.cs.\n      - These changes centralize routing logic around IRoutable, simplify transport implementations, and align event creation with the new routable event types.\n      - Add routing support to core models by implementing IRoutable on PacketModel, RequestModel, and ResponseModel.\n      - Expose MethodRoute and UrlRoute properties for each model (RequestModel uses FirstSpan/SecondSpan, ResponseModel returns protocol/status spans as fallbacks).\n      - PacketModel adds a fixed method route (\"MSG\") and derives UrlRoute from UrlView. Added necessary using directives for LuciferCore.Handler.\n      - These changes enable centralized routing logic to inspect method and URL bytes directly from model instances.",
